<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	AlarmKit needs no entitlement — just NSAlarmKitUsageDescription in Info.plist
	and a runtime AlarmManager.requestAuthorization() call, the same shape as
	Camera/Location/Motion permissions. `com.apple.developer.alarmkit` used to be
	declared here; it isn't a real Apple entitlement (see README.md's AlarmKit
	setup section) and, per a developer forum report, an unrecognized entitlement
	key like that can actually make Xcode reject the provisioning profile on a
	real device build. Left empty on purpose — add real entitlements here only if
	a future feature genuinely needs one (e.g. push notifications, app groups).
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
